<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<%- include('partials/header.ejs') %>

<body>

<div>
    <!--Below is a simple privacy policy tailored for a small
        Canadian website that only collects email addresses for a weekly newsletter.
        It is designed to align with Canada’s federal privacy law framework under
        the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada and general anti-spam requirements
        under Canada’s Anti-Spam Legislation (CASL). You should still consider having a Canadian
        lawyer review it before publishing, especially if the site grows or adds analytics,
        advertising, or additional data collection.-->
    <div class="exjayline"></div>

    <h3 class="exjayheading">Privacy Policy for exbluejays.ca</h3>

    <p>
        Effective Date: May 12, 2026
    </p>

    <p>
        Welcome to exbluejays.ca. We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal information in
        accordance with applicable Canadian privacy laws.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Information We Collect</h4>

    <p>
        We collect only one type of personal information:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>
            Your email address
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        We do not collect names, mailing addresses, payment information, or other personal information.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">How We Use Your Information</h4>

    <p>
        We use your email address solely to:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Send you our weekly email newsletter
        </li>
        <li>
            Communicate updates related to the website or newsletter
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        We do not sell, rent, or share your email address with third parties for marketing purposes.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Consent</h4>

    <p>
        By providing your email address and subscribing to our newsletter, you consent to receiving weekly emails from
        us. You may withdraw your consent at any time by unsubscribing using the unsubscribe link included in our emails
        or by contacting us directly.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Email Service Providers</h4>

    <p>
        We may use a third-party email delivery service (such as Mailchimp, ConvertKit, Substack, or similar providers)
        to manage subscriptions and send emails. Your email address may therefore be stored securely on servers operated
        by those providers. These providers are expected to maintain appropriate security safeguards for your
        information.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Data Retention</h4>

    <p>
        We retain your email address only as long as you remain subscribed to the newsletter or as necessary to comply
        with legal obligations. If you unsubscribe, your email address will be removed from our active mailing list
        within a reasonable period.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Security</h4>

    <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect the email addresses we collect against unauthorized access, disclosure, or
        misuse.  However, no method of electronic storage or transmission over the Internet is completely secure, and we
        cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Cookies and Analytics</h4>

    <p>
        At this time, exbluejays.ca does not intentionally collect additional personal information through cookies,
        analytics tools, or tracking technologies. If this changes in the future, this Privacy Policy will be updated
        accordingly.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Your Rights</h4>

    <p>
        Subject to applicable Canadian law, you may request access to the personal information we hold about you or
        request that it be corrected or deleted.  To make such a request, contact us using the information below.
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Contact</h4>

    <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or your personal information, you may contact:
        <i>feedback@exbluejays.ca</i>
    </p>

    <h4 class="exjayheading">Changes to This Policy</h4>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated
        effective date.
    </p>

</div>
